#: ../../source/docs/common-powermodule-landingpage.rst:9
#: 62b28c2aea3a459c8da9814099addc82
msgid "Power Monitors/Modules provide these benefits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-powermodule-landingpage.rst:11
#: ede39952edbd43fb841ecc9a5d5a8b22
msgid "Most provide a stable power supply to the autopilot, in addition to monitoring, and therefore reduces the chance of a brown-out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-powermodule-landingpage.rst:12
#: 1f7fa171e85d46efac9d77073338f9ea
msgid "Allows real-time monitoring of the battery’s voltage and current and triggering a low battery failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-powermodule-landingpage.rst:13
#: cf401d68756e4246ae98fa343b0c86b6
msgid "Allows compensating for the interference on the compass from the motors using the COMPASS_MOT_x and COMPASS_PMOT_x parameters, see :ref:`common-compass-setup-advanced`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-powermodule-landingpage.rst:15
#: e72cb60cb8be43eda79fc54142ab106b
msgid "The links below have information about the most commonly used power monitors/modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-powermodule-landingpage.rst:17
#: c9baaa2e42ee4b048fbdfee0e9e70a06
msgid "Up to 16 batteries/power monitors can be monitored. Each monitor has its own group of configuration parameters, designated by ``BATTx_`` with x denoting each monitor in the system (first monitor \"x\" is null character, ie ``BATT_`` prefix). In addition, a ``BATT_MONITOR`` \"type\" = SUM is available, that consolidates  battery monitors into a single report using the :ref:`BATT_SUM_MASK<BATT_SUM_MASK>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-powermodule-landingpage.rst:19
#: edcb3f369c044207a4fe9cf356ca4fe6
msgid "some kinds of monitors can provide bi-directional battery current information. These are useful when generators or MPPT chargers are being utilized in the system to monitor the net charge state of the battery."
msgstr ""

